Introduction to React

In simple terms, React is a JavaScript library that helps us create user interfaces (UIs). It

allows us to build UIs by breaking them down into smaller, reusable pieces of code called

components.

A component is like a building block of a UI. It is a JavaScript file that we develop

using TypeScript, which later gets converted into JavaScript. There are parent

components and child components. A child component is a component that is nested

inside another component, which is the parent component. All components maintain

a parent-child relationship. It’s also possible to have a web part consisting of a single

component.

